  "notes": [
    {
      "id": 54,
      "at": [
        -12,
        -20
      ],
      "text": "A 2 Hz clock drives a decade counter (0-9); a CD4511 turns the BCD code into the segments of a\ncommon-cathode display, one 330 ohm resistor per segment. LT and BI go to VCC, LE to ground, and the\n4511 needs its supply on VDD and VSS. Run (F5) at real time and watch it count. Labels join the parts."
    }
  ]
